/* ==========================================================================
 * FR_UNIVERSITIES -- higher education institution directory dataset
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * 1156 institutions from **Idéo-Structures d'enseignement supérieur**, the
 * national register of French higher education institutions published as open
 * data on data.gouv.fr by the ONISEP, the public operator of the Ministère de
 * l'Éducation nationale and the Ministère de l'Enseignement supérieur et de la
 * Recherche. Generated by _tooling/build_dataset_fr.py -- do not hand-edit.
 *
 * WHY THESE INSTITUTIONS AND NOT OTHERS
 *
 * France has no register that IS the permission to enrol an international
 * student -- there is no CRICOS as in Australia and no Code of Practice
 * signatory list as in New Zealand. A VLS-TS "étudiant" is granted on a
 * pre-inscription at a recognised higher education institution, so what is
 * listed here is the national register of those institutions, filtered by the
 * register's own `type_detablissement` column to the ones a foreign applicant
 * can actually apply to.
 *
 * Excluded, deliberately: lycées (the entity is a secondary school); centres
 * de formation d'apprentis (apprenticeship needs a French employment
 * contract); UFR, IUT and INSPE (components of universities already listed, so
 * they would duplicate); écoles de santé and du secteur social (French-language
 * and quota-limited through Parcoursup); and the civil-service schools that
 * recruit by concours. The four écoles normales supérieures and Institut
 * polytechnique de Paris are added back by name -- the register files them
 * under headings the filter drops, but they are degree-granting, admit
 * international students, and three of them are QS-ranked.
 *
 * FIELDS
 *
 *   name      the register's institution name. Where the same name occurs in
 *             more than one commune the commune is appended, because those are
 *             genuinely different campuses to apply to. `uai` carries the
 *             ministry's UAI code, which is the unambiguous key.
 *   sector    the register's own `statut` column -- Public, Private, Private
 *             (contracted) or Private (independent). A REAL published field
 *             with 100% coverage, not a placeholder, and the one that decides
 *             the fee regime: a public institution charges the state-set
 *             inscription fee (€178 licence / €254 master in 2026-27), a private one sets its own. The UI
 *             labels it "Sector" for that reason. (The UK page carries an
 *             invented `offerRate` in this slot; this page does not repeat it.)
 *   programs  the three commonest subject domains across the institution's
 *             entries in the register's own course catalogue (Idéo-Actions de
 *             formation initiale), using its twenty-domain classification.
 *             Indicative, and derived from real data. For the 190
 *             institutions the catalogue does not reach, it falls back to a
 *             descriptor of the institution's REGISTERED TYPE -- still a real
 *             field, simply coarser. It is never a per-institution guess.
 *   type      "Udice" for the 13 members of the published Udice alliance of
 *             French research universities; then "Université", "Grande École",
 *             "Engineering School", "Business School", "Art & Design School"
 *             and "Specialist", all from the register's own type column.
 *   location  the register's commune, plus its INSEE region.
 *   rank      entries 1-38 are the French institutions in the **QS World
 *             University Rankings 2027** (published 18 June 2026), in QS order.
 *             Everything after that is ordered by type tier then name and
 *             carries NO ranking meaning; `ranked` is false for those and the
 *             UI shows a dash rather than a position.
 *   alt       searched, never rendered: acronyms, former names, official
 *             English names and the commune. All but a short list come from
 *             the register itself and from the MESR's `champ_recherche`.
 * ========================================================================== */

